From 97a31e1bd060457ef29d5f11bd3f85473968b409 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincenzo Grimaldi <vince.ceccarelli@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 20:49:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(a11y): clear all 45 axe violations; audit every route in
 CI

The chromedriver fix let axe actually run for the first time, and it
immediately found a real defect. Auditing all 11 routes rather than just
'/' surfaced 45 violation nodes across four distinct causes. All measured
with axe-core 4.13 against a production build; all now zero.

1. heading-order, every page: the footer's column headings were <h4>
   following an <h2>, skipping a level. Promoted to <h2> - valid on every
   page (each has exactly one <h1>, and returning from h3 to h2 is allowed;
   only forward skips violate the rule).

2. heading-order, /work and /404: the card grid jumped <h1> to <h3> with no
   <h2> between. Those two routes now render card titles as <h2> via
   .work-card-title; the homepage teaser keeps <h3> because an <h2> section
   heading precedes it there.

3. color-contrast, every page: the consent banner inherited the light-theme
   --link (#0972d3) onto a near-black panel - 3.98:1. Now an explicit
   #7dd3fc at 11.5:1, underlined. Separately --link itself measured 4.37:1
   on --card-bg (#f2f3f3), just under the 4.5 threshold, so it moves to
   #0b5cad: 6.05:1 on cards, 6.67:1 on white, no perceptible hue change.

4. color-contrast, /capabilities: the physics formula panel used a
   translucent dark fill over a light card, compositing to mid-grey while
   the text stayed dark. Replaced the inline styles with .formula-block -
   opaque #0b1220 ground, #e2e8f0 text at 15.19:1, subscripts at 12.61:1.

5. link-in-text-block, /impressum: the ODR link inside a paragraph was
   distinguishable by colour alone. Legal prose links are now underlined.

CI now runs axe across all ten public routes instead of the homepage
alone, so none of this can regress silently.

Verified: 0 violation nodes on / /work /work/cim-threma /capabilities
/simulator /payments /connect /card /impressum /datenschutz /404.
typecheck, lint, build and scripts/verify.sh all clean. Dependency tree
unchanged - the Playwright-based auditor used to measure this was local
tooling and is not committed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
